{
  "info": {
    "name": "jWallet Lite API",
    "_postman_id": "6f1f3a4e-2c1b-4c8e-9b7a-1a2b3c4d5e6f",
    "description": "Mock REST API for the jWallet Lite Flutter app.\n\nEvery response (success and error) uses the envelope:\n`{ \"meta\": { \"statusCode\", \"message\" }, \"body\": { ... } }`. Errors put `errorCode` (and `details` for validation) in `body`.\n\n**Quick start:** pick an environment (or edit the `baseUrl` collection variable), run **Auth → Login**, then any request. Tokens are saved automatically.\n\n**Transfers are two steps:** *1. Create transfer challenge* (saves `challengeId` and a fresh `idempotencyKey`), then *2. Transfer with PIN*. The user needs a PIN first: run **Security → Set PIN** within 5 minutes of logging in (once per user).\n\n**Encryption:** the mobile app encrypts bodies end-to-end (ECDH P-256 + HKDF + AES-256-GCM, header `X-Encrypted: 1`). The server also accepts plain JSON, which is what this collection sends. Run `npm run demo:encrypted` to see encrypted calls.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
